{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"publicized-chuffy-guanaco","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Symptom\n\n`docs/orphaned-processes.md` (lines 11-16) still carries the exact pattern that bug\n`0d6c-b19b-0de7-432e` removed from AGENTS.md:\n\n```sh\ntimeout 120 python -c 'while True: pass' &\ntrap 'kill 0' EXIT INT TERM\n```\n\nand the prose still asserts that \"the trap signals the process group on normal exit, interruption,\nor error\". Both claims were disproved on a macOS host on 2026-09-04:\n\n- `timeout` and `gtimeout` are absent; the line exits 127 and the helper never starts.\n- `( trap 'kill 0' EXIT INT TERM; sleep 1 )` in a plain script killed the **script** (rc 143,\n  SIGTERM), because a subshell shares its parent's process group -- while a wrapper shell above the\n  script is never in that group and survives. That wrapper is the process that leaked.\n\nAGENTS.md now links to this document for incident evidence and recovery, so a reader who follows the\npointer lands back on the defective prescription.\n\n## Why it was not fixed with the parent\n\n`0d6c-b19b-0de7-432e` declared `file_impact: AGENTS.md` only, and widening file impact mid-flight\ninvalidates a signed plan-review attestation. Split out rather than smuggled in.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `docs/orphaned-processes.md` no longer prescribes a bare `timeout` as the bound; it uses the\n  host-selecting `bound()` form now in AGENTS.md, or points at it instead of restating it.\n- [ ] The `trap 'kill 0'` line and the \"signals the process group\" sentence are removed or corrected\n  to say what the group actually is. Checked with `grep -n \"kill 0\" docs/orphaned-processes.md`.\n- [ ] The two documents agree: `grep -n 'timeout\\|kill 0' AGENTS.md docs/orphaned-processes.md`\n  shows no surviving contradiction.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Re-run the demonstrations recorded on `0d6c-b19b-0de7-432e` against whatever the corrected\n  document prescribes, on a macOS host, and paste the output.\n- `make lint`, `make typecheck`.\n\n## File impact\n\n`docs/orphaned-processes.md`.","id":"6a9d-4792-7099-4a17","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["docs","agents","portability","process-hygiene"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"docs/orphaned-processes.md still prescribes bare timeout and trap 'kill 0', the pattern removed from AGENTS.md"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788548813075987001,"uuid":"c82e3237-e78d-4aa6-ae49-331c3b16a848"}